{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqq2d9u1f7x","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"bench judge drain needs api backend not agentic cli","summary":"P3 de-ported the bench edge judge: the canonical ON arm (arms.run_canonical_wiring) now drives the production sync judge via POST /judge/drain (P1) instead of running its own EdgeJudge; EdgeJudge + the hand-copied keep/prune rubric are deleted from bench/zonoid_bench/judge.py. Verified finding: P1's runJudgeDrainSync (lib/headless-drain.js ~1404) unconditionally calls provider.runJudgeLoop, which ONLY the api-kind backend (OpenRouter, lib/llm-backend.js) implements. The default claude backend is kind agentic-cli and has NO runJudgeLoop, so /judge/drain returns HTTP 500 (TypeError) when the daemon is authed only via CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN; it returns skipped:no_backend when no backend is authed at all. So the bench smoke (A1/A2) only goes green when the embedded bench daemon has an api backend authed (OPENROUTER_API_KEY set). This environment has neither OPENROUTER_API_KEY nor ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — only an OAuth token selecting the un-drainable agentic-cli path — so the production judge cannot run and A1/A2 cannot pass here. Also: smoke.py _find_daemon_js picks the worktree with node_modules; only the main checkout (D:/zonoid, on main) has node_modules but it lacks P1's /judge/drain, so the embedded daemon must run the feature-branch daemon.js (junction node_modules into the attempt worktree, or install node_modules there).","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-23T03:07:29.929Z","vec":[-0.0796770378947258,0.04037755727767944,-0.10038155317306519,-0.03540455549955368,0.012455866672098637,-0.06358354538679123,-0.047796960920095444,0.041989486664533615,-0.008797700516879559,0.02399061620235443,-0.0032049803994596004,0.016429167240858078,0.029934896156191826,-0.047268208116292953,0.03125675395131111,0.057410433888435364,0.08123162388801575,0.01678432710468769,-0.004142592195421457,0.00088541605509817